  "narrative": "I use the controller's signed convention throughout. For direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has the more negative, stronger-dependency composite score in the claimed direction; for direction +1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has the less negative, weaker-dependency score in the claimed direction. The newly released validation evidence materially sharpens the main conclusions. H4, SMARCA4 loss overall in screen-quality-eligible lines, is independently validated: R13 is +0.760 with the stringent validation interval [0.666, 0.854], entirely above the 0.15-unit threshold and consistent with discovery R4 +0.824 [0.755, 0.893]. Therefore SMARCA4 loss remains the strongest supported dataset association: SMARCA4-loss cells have much more negative composite dependency scores. I accept H4 and close that main claim. H29, TP53 loss in stricter screen-quality lines, is also independently validated: R40 is +0.549 with validation interval [0.362, 0.736], fully above threshold, and consistent with discovery R20 +0.462 [0.342, 0.583]. Thus TP53 loss is supported as a dataset-specific association with less negative composite scores, especially under high screen-quality eligibility. I accept H29 and close that strict-quality main claim. The adenocarcinoma-context result is not supported as a context interaction. H34 tested the original direction that SMARCA4 loss would associate with even stronger negative dependency in adenocarcinoma; R37 was in the opposite direction and the newly delivered validation R39 is signed -0.084 with interval [-0.310, 0.141], neither in the claimed direction nor above threshold. I therefore reject H34 and close it. The reversed claim H56, attenuation of the SMARCA4-loss association in adenocarcinoma, remains unresolved rather than accepted: discovery R37 was +0.237 but its interval started at +0.082, and validation R39 is only +0.084 with interval [-0.141, 0.310]. The point estimate in validation is below the practical threshold and the interval includes both null and threshold-range effects. Thus the data do not establish adenocarcinoma-specific attenuation; they leave it as an uncertain, possibly small context effect. The direct adenocarcinoma mean effect and a TP53/KEAP1-intact adenocarcinoma interaction check are registered to resolve whether the main SMARCA4 association persists within adenocarcinoma and whether any context signal is confounded by correlated losses. These conclusions remain dataset-specific associations. The strongest accepted predictors are now SMARCA4 loss with much stronger dependency, TP53 loss with weaker dependency, KEAP1 loss with weaker dependency, and PTEN loss with moderately stronger dependency. PTEN remains the least certain accepted main effect because its validation interval crossed the 0.15 threshold at the lower bound, but the discovery and validation point estimates replicated and the co-occurrence checks H42 and H45 support marker specificity. CDKN2A remains borderline and unresolved: main R18 is +0.144 [0.060, 0.228], strict high-quality R30 is +0.130 [0.020, 0.240], while TP53/KEAP1-intact R31 is +0.155 [0.082, 0.228]; none is decisively above threshold. The most informative next analyses are direct quantification of SMARCA4 within adenocarcinoma and in cleaner TP53/KEAP1-intact adenocarcinoma context, stricter CDKN2A checks that also exclude SMARCA4 loss, PTEN high-quality robustness, SMARCA4 specificity against ARID1A, and the lower-threshold STK11-hypoxia follow-up. Context checks for TP53 with high ploidy and KEAP1 with high aneuploidy are also registered because they test whether the accepted weaker-dependency associations persist in genomically unstable cells. All reported effects are associations in the supplied dataset and do not establish causality, biological mechanism, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Current round-3 synthesis after validations. Signed convention: direction -1 positive = stronger/more negative dependency; direction +1 positive = weaker/less negative dependency. Robust accepted core: SMARCA4_loss more negative (H4 accepted, validated R13 +0.760 [0.666,0.854]; discovery R4; co-occurrence robust); TP53_loss less negative (H13 accepted; H29 strict-quality accepted and validated R40 +0.549 [0.362,0.736]); KEAP1_loss less negative (H14 accepted; H30 strict-quality R21 +0.788 [0.703,0.874], co-occurrence robust); PTEN_loss more negative (H16 accepted, validated but lower bound near threshold; specificity supported by H42 and H45). Closed support checks: H22 ARID1A among SMARCA4-intact null; H42 PTEN among SMARCA4-intact; H45 PTEN among TP53/KEAP1-intact; H48-H51 co-occurring subgroup main effects; H32 SMARCA4 x serum interaction null; H52 PIK3CA null. Adenocarcinoma context: H34 original interaction wrong direction, rejected/closed; H56 reversed attenuation remains unresolved active because discovery was borderline and validation R39 +0.084 [-0.141,0.310] failed to support threshold effect. Do not claim attenuation yet. Next priorities: H57 direct SMARCA4 main within adenocarcinoma; newly proposed high-quality adeno SMARCA4 main; newly proposed SMARCA4 adeno interaction with TP53-intact and KEAP1-intact to remove correlated opposite losses. CDKN2A: H58 strict high-quality TP53/KEAP1-intact and newly proposed strict high-quality TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact should resolve borderline. PTEN: H43 high-quality PTEN. SMARCA4 specificity: H21 SMARCA4 among ARID1A-intact. STK11: H27 lower hypoxia interaction and newly proposed direct STK11 mean in hypoxia>=0.75. Contexts: TP53 high ploidy and KEAP1 high aneuploidy proposed; H31/H33/H35/H36/H37 remain. Assay context: H38 media main, H39 library main. Remaining broad molecular: H53-H55 plus newly registered ERBB2, BRAF, MSI, BRCA2. Negative/nulls so far include KRAS, STK11 main, ARID1A main and SMARCA4-intact check, RB1, MTAP, SMAD4, MYC amp, PIK3CA, research marker main effects and marker-signature interactions. All claims are dataset-specific associations only."
